## 2. Kernel & System Version (Vuln Matching)
`uname`, `rpm` all work as non-root.

```bash
uname -a
uname -r
cat /proc/version
cat /etc/redhat-release 2>/dev/null
rpm -q kernel                          # All installed kernels
rpm -qa | grep -iE 'kernel|glibc|openssl|sudo'   # Patch level
```

Compare `uname -r` against local exploit DB / `linux-exploit-suggester`.

