## 3. SUID / SGID Binaries (Readable to You)
`find` works without root — you just won't see into dirs you can't traverse.

```bash
# SUID
find / -xdev -type f -perm -4000 -ls 2>/dev/null

# SGID
find / -xdev -type f -perm -2000 -ls 2>/dev/null

# Both, excluding common false-positives
find / -xdev -type f \( -perm -4000 -o -perm -2000 \) -ls 2>/dev/null | grep -vE '/proc|/sys'
```

Then cross-reference hits with **GTFOBins**: `https://gtfobins.github.io/`

