## 4. Writable Paths (As Current User)
This is the core of local privesc — what can *you* modify?

```bash
# World-writable directories
find / -xdev -type d -perm -o+w -ls 2>/dev/null

# World-writable files (careful — can be noisy)
find / -xdev -type f -perm -o+w -ls 2>/dev/null

# Files/dirs owned by YOU and writable
find / -xdev \( -user "$(id -u)" -o -group "$(id -g)" \) -writable -ls 2>/dev/null

# Writable directories in PATH (classic hijack)
IFS=:; for d in $PATH; do [ -w "$d" ] && echo "[!] WRITABLE IN PATH: $d"; done; unset IFS

# Writable cron scripts (user crons + system crons if readable)
find /etc/cron* /var/spool/cron* -type f -writable 2>/dev/null
crontab -l 2>/dev/null
cat /etc/crontab 2>/dev/null
ls -la /etc/cron.d/ /etc/cron.daily/ /etc/cron.hourly/ 2>/dev/null
```

