## 5. Writable Scripts (Privesc Vectors)
Scripts *you* can edit that are likely run by root or a privileged process.

```bash
find / -xdev -type f \( -name "*.sh" -o -name "*.py" -o -name "*.pl" -o -name "*.rb" \) \
  -writable -ls 2>/dev/null

# Scripts run by root, but that you can write (look for owner=root, writable by you)
find /opt /usr/local /var /srv /home -type f -writable \
  -not -user "$(id -un)" -ls 2>/dev/null
```

