## 6. SSH / RSA Key Leaks (Readable Only)
Only keys readable by your user are returned.

```bash
# Search home dirs + common locations, only readable files
find /home /root /etc /opt /srv /var/www -maxdepth 5 -type f \
  \( -name "id_rsa" -o -name "id_dsa" -o -name "id_ecdsa" -o -name "id_ed25519" \
     -o -name "*.pem" -o -name "*.key" -o -name "*.ppk" -o -name "authorized_keys" \
     -o -name "known_hosts" \) -readable -ls 2>/dev/null

# Look for private keys by content in readable files
grep -rlE "BEGIN (RSA|OPENSSH|EC|DSA|PRIVATE) KEY" /home /opt /var/www /etc /srv 2>/dev/null

# SSH agent / config that YOU can access
ls -la ~/.ssh/ 2>/dev/null
env | grep -i ssh
```

