## 7. Hardcoded Credentials (Readable Config / Scripts)
Only files your user can read are scanned.

```bash
# Web app configs (WordPress, Laravel, Django, generic)
find /var/www /srv /opt /usr/local /etc -maxdepth 6 -type f \
  \( -name "wp-config.php" -o -name "config.php" -o -name "*.env" -o -name ".env*" \
     -o -name "settings.py" -o -name "database.yml" -o -name "*.ini" \
     -o -name "config.json" -o -name "*.conf" \) -readable 2>/dev/null

# Grep readable config/scripts for creds
grep -rilE "(pass(word|wd)?|secret|token|api[_-]?key|db_pass|root_pass)\s*[:=]" \
  /var/www /opt /srv /etc /home 2>/dev/null | head -50

# Extract from readable binaries (rarely useful but cheap)
find / -xdev -type f -executable -readable 2>/dev/null | head -200 | \
  xargs -I{} sh -c 'strings "{}" 2>/dev/null | grep -qi "password" && echo "{}"' 2>/dev/null

# History files — goldmine
cat ~/.bash_history 2>/dev/null | grep -iE "pass|mysql -p|ssh |sudo "
find /home -maxdepth 3 -name ".*history" -readable 2>/dev/null
```

