## 8. Sensitive File Exposure (Permission Check, Not Contents)
We check *if* you can read them — not force-read.

```bash
for f in /etc/shadow /etc/gshadow /etc/sudoers /etc/ssh/sshd_config \
         /root/.ssh/id_rsa /root/.bash_history /var/log/auth.log \
         /var/log/secure /var/log/messages; do
  [ -e "$f" ] && { [ -r "$f" ] && echo "[+] READABLE: $f" || echo "[-] $f"; }
done

# Any readable file in /root
find /root -maxdepth 3 -readable -ls 2>/dev/null

# World-writable sensitive system files
find /etc /bin /sbin /usr/bin /usr/sbin -xdev -not -type l -perm -o+w -ls 2>/dev/null
```

